   "body": "Adversarial review (Opus 5.5), round 1, head 4b00582, verbatim:\n\n**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5): APPROVE** — head 4b00582\n\nFindings\n1. Detail, process (outside the diff): issue #800 also asks whether CI shows these warnings, why it does not if so, and for a proposed (not applied) step that fails the build on new warnings. Nothing in the diff covers this, which is expected since it is not a code change. Make sure the PR body answers it, or say it is left for later (`Refs #800` instead of `Closes #800`).\n\nNo defects found in the code.\n\n- `NotificationLedgerStore.swift:37,50`: `_ =` is the right fix. Neither caller needs the result. `recordNews` returns the diff it captured, and `markCheckedIfDue` returns `due`, which it captures before the `&&` short-circuit. Marking the private `update` `@discardableResult` would have hidden the result from any future caller too. Behaviour is unchanged.\n- `ForumScopeBar.swift:10`: `@MainActor (TopicSource) -> Void` is the isolation the closure really runs with.\n  - The only producer, `NavigationModel.scope(for:)` (`NavigationModel.swift:103-111`), is a method of a `@MainActor` class, and its closure writes main-actor state.\n  - The only consumer is the `Binding(set:)` in `body`, which also runs on the main actor. There is no other caller or test that builds a `ForumScope`.\n  - Under SE-0434, global-actor-isolated function types are implicitly `Sendable`. So converting it to `@isolated(any) @Sendable` keeps the main-actor isolation instead of dropping it.\n  - `TopicSource` is `Hashable, Sendable` (`TopicSource.swift:5`).\n  - The app builds as Swift 6.0 with strict concurrency set to `complete`.\n  - This is a cause-level fix, with no `nonisolated(unsafe)` or `@preconcurrency`.\n\n**Verified**\n- HFRStorage built on Linux at base `origin/dev-swift`: the two `result of call to 'update' is unused` warnings at `:37` and `:50`. At the head: 0 warnings in HFRKit Sources.\n- `swift build --build-tests` at the head: the only remaining warnings are in test files outside #800's scope (redundant `#require`, an ambiguous requirement, an `await` with no async call).\n- `swift test --filter NotificationLedger`: 21/21 passed.\n- SwiftLint 0.65.1 on both changed files: clean.\n- App target not built (Linux). Judged from source as described above.\n\nAuthor note: `swift test` in `Packages/HFRKit`: 1940 tests passed. Finding 1 is handled by switching the PR to `Refs #800` (the CI-warnings question stays open on the issue).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
